\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces  TETHER at three scales. \textbf  {(a)} Bounded recurrence: memory carries the \emph  {fused} disparity forward, and every $H{=}4$ frames the chain is cut and re-tied to raw geometry the frozen network produced independently (teal). The five frames are consecutive and the two disparity rows share one colour scale, differing by $0.126$\,px on average. One fitted plane is removed from all ten disparity panels: the surface is smooth at this resolution, a $7$\,px depth ramp carrying about $1$\,px of anatomy, so an absolute rendering shows a gradient and no scene. The same plane is subtracted from both rows, so the difference between them is untouched. \textbf  {(b)} One time step; dashed grey is frozen, the single orange block is the only trained component and emits one scalar per pixel, $w_t$, rather than geometry. \textbf  {(c)} The evidence space: none of the $38$ channels carries ground truth, backbone identity or a future frame, and none is produced by a learned feature extractor. }}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:system}{{1}{3}{}{}{}}
\newlabel{eq:fb}{{1}{3}{}{}{}}
